  I've been meaning to post a recent-ish project of mine where I ran
  OCaml (and much more) on a 1960s UNIVAC 1219B! The demo I chose to run
  was a sudoku solver. In short, this was done by compiling OCaml to C,
  C to RISC-V, and then emulating RISC-V on the UNIVAC.

