<div id=3D"outline-container-orge8f01ac" class=3D"outline-3">
<h3 id=3D"orge8f01ac">Nathan Farlow announced</h3>
<div class=3D"outline-text-3" id=3D"text-orge8f01ac">
<p>
Hi!
</p>

<p>
I've been meaning to post a recent-ish project of mine where I ran OCaml (a=
nd much more) on a 1960s UNIVAC 1219B! The demo I chose to run was a sudoku=
 solver. In short, this was done by compiling OCaml to C, C to RISC-V, and =
then emulating RISC-V on the UNIVAC.
</p>

<p>
Full UNIVAC toolchain: <a href=3D"https://farlow.dev/2026/04/17/running-a-m=
inecraft-server-and-more-on-a-1960s-univac-computer">Writeup</a>, and <a hr=
ef=3D"https://github.com/nathanfarlow/univac-1219-riscv">source</a>. Please=
 see the my comment below for the other links! I'm unable to post more than=
 two links in a post.
</p>

<p>
I also ran an OCaml program submitted by a friend that computed factors of =
numbers. At one point we thought the program crashed, but we were delighted=
 when the program resumed ~5 minutes later. Turns out garbage collecting is=
 slow on this machine :slight_smile:
</p>

<p>
Oh, and it works with OxCaml too!
</p>

<p>
Enjoy! Below are some pictures. (Disregard the earlier output, that was a r=
un of ELIZA :slight_smile:)
